    `merge_after` schema field is NOT introduced in the WCI-1+WCI-2 MVP).
  - §5.1 — the SEMANTIC-INDEPENDENCE PROOF contract (import-graph reachability + shared-symbol +
    shared-config + test co-failure) — strictly STRONGER than owns-disjointness. The keystone:
    nothing slices concurrently without it (the F1 invariant: a label flip is never a downgrade;
    the split is invented by the proof, never by the label).
  - WCI-6 — auto-slice / decomposer execution, gated behind §5.1 AND the ADR-0008 Phase-2
    conflict-rate tripwire.
  (WCI-5, the semantic ADVISORY pass, is a SEPARATELY-gated new-value spike — NOT in this group.)
